  "body": "A compelling opportunity awaits developers, builders and land bankers in the heart of Mission Bay. Both 49 and 51 Nihill Crescent are zoned Residential Mixed Housing Urban, offering excellent scope to explore future development possibilities, subject to the usual council approvals and purchaser due diligence. Offered for sale by Tender, buyers have the flexibility to secure either property individually or purchase both together.\r\n49 Nihill Crescent comprises approximately 809sqm of fee simple vacant land, providing a rare blank canvas in this established neighbourhood. Neighbouring 51 Nihill Crescent sits on approximately 817sqm of fee simple land and includes an existing 1940s three-bedroom home, offering holding potential while future plans are considered.\r\nThe location adds further strength to this offering, with Mission Bay’s beach, cafes, restaurants and everyday amenities all within easy reach. Convenient transport connections provide access to Auckland CBD, while the area is also well served by established local schools, including Kohimarama School and Selwyn College.\r\nWith a motivated vendor and clear instructions to sell, this is an opportunity to secure one or two substantial Mission Bay landholdings with genuine future potential.  View by appointment.\r\nTo be sold by Tender, Closing at 4pm, 27 October 2026 at 421 Tamaki Drive, St Heliers\r\nContact Murray today for further information.",
